- `System.Xml.Serialization.XmlSerializer` wraps collections by default. This serializer doesn't, so add `[XmlArray]` when you need XML that matches what that serializer produced.
- The default item name is the .NET type name of the item, such as `Int32`, `String`, or the name of your class, converted by the element naming policy.
- `[XmlPropertyName]` on the same member takes precedence over `ElementName`, and `[XmlPropertyOrder]` and `[XmlElement(Order = n)]` take precedence over `Order`.
- A `null` wrapped collection is written as the wrapper marked `xsi:nil="true"`. It is left out when the ignore condition that applies to the member is `WhenWritingNull` or `WhenWritingDefault`.
- The attribute applies to collections. A dictionary is always written inside an element named after the member, without it.
